;; Nigeria (federal) public holidays 2016-2040: external gold for NG.
;; Regenerate: uv run --no-project --with holidays==0.109 python -I scripts/generate_mena_holiday_gold.py NG
;; :days lists every holiday as (YEAR MONTH DAY NAME); any other day is not one.
(
 :country "NG"
 :generated "2026-11-28"
 :from 2016 :to 2040
 :note "Federal public holidays of Nigeria: the Public Holidays Act (Decree 1979 No. 3 as amended; Democracy Day 29 May 2000-2018, 12 June from 2019), at the days the Ministry of Interior declared 2016-2026 (interior.gov.ng releases): the Eid and Maulud days and the next working days declared for weekend holidays (no statutory in-lieu rule, s. 5(b)). 2027-2040 are provisional: the statutory days and tabular Eid el-Fitr, Eid el-Kabir (2 days) and Maulud."
 :weekends ((nil 6 7))
 :sources
 (
  (:title "Public Holidays Decree 1979 (Decree No. 3 of 1979)" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20240616072641/https://archive.gazettes.africa/archive/ng/1979/ng-government-gazette-supplement-dated-1979-02-01-no-5.pdf"
   :text "s.1 days in the Schedule are public holidays throughout Nigeria; s.2(1) Head of FMG (now President) may by public notice appoint special days (s.2(3): incl. work-free days); s.3 Commissioner (Minister) for Internal Affairs may substitute another day; s.5(b) a holiday on Saturday or Sunday gets NO day in lieu; s.5(d) Sunday+Monday pair -> only the Monday. Schedule: New Year's Day, Good Friday, Easter Monday, National Day (1 Oct), Christmas Day, and 'such day as the Commissioner may declare' for Id el Fitr, Id el Kabir and Id el Maulud (one day each in the text). No Boxing Day in the Schedule.")
  (:title "Public Holidays (Amendment) Decree 1984 (Decree No. 26 of 1984)" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20240615185836/https://archive.gazettes.africa/archive/ng/1984/ng-government-gazette-supplement-dated-1984-08-30-no-52-part-a.pdf"
   :text "Inserts 'Workers' day (1st May)' as Schedule para. 4.")
  (:title "Public Holidays (Amendment) Act 2000 (cited in the LFN 2004 Schedule note as '2000 No. 81' - OCR, unverified)" :uri "https://placng.org/lawsofnigeria/view2.php?sn=467"
   :text "Adds Democracy Day (29 May) to the Schedule (first observed 29 May 2000).")
  (:title "President Buhari declares June 12 the new Democracy Day (State House statement)" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20250829060151/https://statehouse.gov.ng/news/president-buhari-declares-june-12-the-new-democracy-day/"
   :text "June 12 'in future years will replace May 29th as a National Public Holiday'; 12 June 2018 itself was a commemoration, not a holiday.")
  (:title "Public Holidays (Amendment) Act 2019 (June 12 Democracy Day)" :uri "https://www.thisdaylive.com/2019/06/11/buhari-signs-june-12-bill-into-law/"
   :text "Replaces 'Democracy Day (29th May)' with 'Democracy Day (12th June)'. 29 May ceases to be a holiday (but is declared work-free in inauguration years).")
  (:title "Annual Federal Ministry of Interior declarations (press releases) under ss. 2-3 of the Act" :uri "https://fmino.gov.ng/wp-json/wp/v2/posts?search=public%20holiday"
   :text "Every year the Minister declares: Boxing Day (26 Dec) although not in the Schedule; two days for each Eid (Fitr, Kabir); one day for Maulud; and, despite s.5, a weekday in lieu (normally the Monday) when a holiday falls on a Saturday or Sunday (seen 2011, 2015-2025).")
  (:title "FG declares Friday 25th and Monday 28th March 2016 public holidays (Easter) (Federal Ministry of Interior press release) (2016)" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20170118122949/http://interior.gov.ng/index.php/84-press-release/167-eastercelebrations"
   :text "")
